      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given that the geometric mean (GM) of two positive real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is \\(\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3}\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3} \\implies ab = 3\n\\]\nThe harmonic mean (HM) of two positive real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{HM} = \\frac{2ab}{a + b}\n\\]\nWe are given that the harmonic mean is \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\), so:\n\\[\n\\frac{2ab}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(ab = 3\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2} \\implies \\frac{6}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2} \\implies 6 \\cdot 2 = 3 \\cdot (a + b) \\implies 12 = 3(a + b) \\implies a + b = 4\n\\]\nNow we have a system of equations:\n\\[\nab = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad a + b = 4\n\\]\nWe can solve this system by treating \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) as the roots of the quadratic equation \\(x^2 - (a+b)x + ab = 0\\). Substituting the known values, we get:\n\\[\nx^2 - 4x + 3 = 0\n\\]\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = -4\\), and \\(c = 3\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{16 - 12}}{2} = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{4}}{2} = \\frac{4 \\pm 2}{2}\n\\]\nThis gives us the solutions:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{4 + 2}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = \\frac{4 - 2}{2} = 1\n\\]\nTherefore, the two numbers are \\(1\\) and \\(3\\). The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1, 3}\n\\]",
